+t.$ Then, $1+3t=3u-2$ and $\\textrm{d}u = \\textrm d t.$ We also need to compute new limits, given below.\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =6\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+3t)\\sqrt{1+t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}(3u-2)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{u}^{3/2}-2{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\pi \\cdot {[\\frac{6{u}^{5/2}}{5}-\\frac{4{u}^{3/2}}{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =6\\pi [(\\frac{6({2}^{5/2})}{5}-\\frac{4({2}^{3/2})}{3})-(\\frac{6}{5}-\\frac{4}{3})] \\\\  & =6\\pi [(\\frac{24\\sqrt{2}}{5}-\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{3})-(\\frac{6}{5}-\\frac{4}{3})] \\\\  & =6\\pi [\\frac{32\\sqrt{2}}{15}+\\frac{2}{15}] \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{5}(16\\sqrt{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536176 true] [17592186129250 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387334 13194139536176 true] [17592186129250 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387390 13194139536176 true] [17592186129250 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387397 13194139536176 true] [17592186129251 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387362 13194139536176 true] [17592186129251 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387369 13194139536176 true] [17592186129251 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387376 13194139536176 true] [17592186129251 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387383 13194139536176 true] [17592186129252 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387341 13194139536176 true] [17592186129252 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387348 13194139536176 true] [17592186129252 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387355 13194139536176 true] [17592186129252 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387404 13194139536176 true] [17592186129252 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387407 13194139536176 true] [17592186129422 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536176 true] [17592186129422 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$x = \\cos 2t, y = \\cos t, t ∈ [0, \\frac{π}{4}]$.\nWhat integral gives the surface area generated when this curve is rotated $2π$ radians about the $x$-axis?" 13194139536176 false] [17592186129422 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=\\o